(6405080, 949420, 129267, '<td valign="top">nice shot. I think I would have tried reversing the order of the lemon wedge and salt, as there appears to be a much stronger highlight on the right side of only the first glass. The liquid in the middle glass feels a bit colorless, giving impressions of water. the reflection of the lemon adds some wonderful contrast though.</td>', 'nice shot. I think I would have tried reversing the order of the lemon wedge and salt, as there appears to be a much stronger highlight on the right side of only the first glass. The liquid in the middle glass feels a bit colorless, giving impressions of water. the reflection of the lemon adds some wonderful contrast though.', '2011-05-05 15:20:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6405084, 948548, 129267, '<td valign="top">everything feels a bit haphazardly placed, which brings some of the atmosphere of the shot down some. the most interesting part of the image is the right side of the right-most blue drink, there''s either some flame or smoke, or something there, but it looks lovely. The glasses feel a bit flat in contrast, maybe some form of a side or hair light could be used to make the lip shine?</td>', 'everything feels a bit haphazardly placed, which brings some of the atmosphere of the shot down some. the most interesting part of the image is the right side of the right-most blue drink, there''s either some flame or smoke, or something there, but it looks lovely. The glasses feel a bit flat in contrast, maybe some form of a side or hair light could be used to make the lip shine?', '2011-05-05 15:23:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6405085, 948534, 129267, '<td valign="top">if they served drinks in a hospital waiting room, this would be it. the greenish grey-blue color cast is very sterile. the bubbles in the drink being poured are interesting to me, as are the side-reflections in the glasses themselves. <br/> <br/>Not sure about the title, as there aren''t people in the scene.</td>', 'if they served drinks in a hospital waiting room, this would be it. the greenish grey-blue color cast is very sterile. the bubbles in the drink being poured are interesting to me, as are the side-reflections in the glasses themselves.  Not sure about the title, as there aren''t people in the scene.', '2011-05-05 15:25:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(6405087, 949743, 129267, '<td valign="top">I think this would be more impactful just a bit more brightly exposed/blown out with some more saturation. it''s a fun party-type photo, but it doesn''t really feel too exciting, despite being on an angle.</td>', 'I think this would be more impactful just a bit more brightly exposed/blown out with some more saturation. it''s a fun party-type photo, but it doesn''t really feel too exciting, despite being on an angle.', '2011-05-05 15:28:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6405089, 949731, 129267, '<td valign="top">heh, i have those same placemats, I believe.<br/> <br/>For me this is missing just a hair more lighting in the glass itself, maybe from the left side, so that the front is still in darkness.</td>', 'heh, i have those same placemats, I believe. For me this is missing just a hair more lighting in the glass itself, maybe from the left side, so that the front is still in darkness.', '2011-05-05 15:30:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(6405094, 949633, 129267, '<td valign="top">This feels a bit strange on a few levels. It seems to lean just a bit to the left, but that just might be my eyes. I also think the reflection is given a bit too much real-estate on the page. It''s not bright enough or sharp enough to be interesting, maybe if this was shot on a mirror, that''d be different. <br/> <br/>the main thing that I noticed, and is probably what''s going to hurt your score a bit from the other voters is that the lighting is causing some really strange highlights on the glasses, while simultaneously making the scene feel very flat/low contrast. If these glasses were lit from one side (and have a black card as your bounce on the other side) you get really strong contrast, and a nice looking vertical stripe on the side of the glasses.</td>', 'This feels a bit strange on a few levels. It seems to lean just a bit to the left, but that just might be my eyes. I also think the reflection is given a bit too much real-estate on the page. It''s not bright enough or sharp enough to be interesting, maybe if this was shot on a mirror, that''d be different.  the main thing that I noticed, and is probably what''s going to hurt your score a bit from the other voters is that the lighting is causing some really strange highlights on the glasses, while simultaneously making the scene feel very flat/low contrast. If these glasses were lit from one side (and have a black card as your bounce on the other side) you get really strong contrast, and a nice looking vertical stripe on the side of the glasses.', '2011-05-05 15:34:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6405095, 948344, 129267, '<td valign="top">I can read bacardi, but I''d really like to be able to see the labels a bit more clearly of the other liquor. I like the sepia, and the dirty glass. the reflection feels natural in this one as well. The odd shaped wooden things are trying to steal the show from the bottles on the left side as well.</td>', 'I can read bacardi, but I''d really like to be able to see the labels a bit more clearly of the other liquor. I like the sepia, and the dirty glass. the reflection feels natural in this one as well. The odd shaped wooden things are trying to steal the show from the bottles on the left side as well.', '2011-05-05 15:36:53.000000', NULL, 1),
