(6410235, 949475, 96751, '<td valign="top">So exactly how many hands DO you have!!??  Fabulous shot. Congrats on the blue.  Although this could also have worked for gold :-)</td>', 'So exactly how many hands DO you have!!??  Fabulous shot. Congrats on the blue.  Although this could also have worked for gold :-)', '2011-05-11 03:38:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(6410236, 949542, 96751, '<td valign="top">Love it, Karen.  This is a type of photography I''ve totally given up on because it''s so tough.  So kudos to you, and congrats on the top 10</td>', 'Love it, Karen.  This is a type of photography I''ve totally given up on because it''s so tough.  So kudos to you, and congrats on the top 10', '2011-05-11 03:40:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(6410237, 949489, 124875, '<td valign="top">Thank you everybody!<br/>@jamesgoss: I must confess: I didn''t read any dictionary, so when I took this photo I didn''t know exactly what a "shotglass" is. I thought that it was just a way of saying "take a picture (shot) of a glass that it''s not a wine glass", or something like that. When I finally saw the others'' pictures, I understood, but it was too late! :-)<br/>Yes, Karen, you''re right: the glass should have been cleaner, and maybe newer, too.<br/>Conclusion: I have to be more careful the next time!<br/>Your suggestions have been very useful: thank you<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-05-11 02:44:20.</i></td>', 'Thank you everybody!@jamesgoss: I must confess: I didn''t read any dictionary, so when I took this photo I didn''t know exactly what a "shotglass" is. I thought that it was just a way of saying "take a picture (shot) of a glass that it''s not a wine glass", or something like that. When I finally saw the others'' pictures, I understood, but it was too late! :-)Yes, Karen, you''re right: the glass should have been cleaner, and maybe newer, too.Conclusion: I have to be more careful the next time!Your suggestions have been very useful: thank you', '2011-05-11 03:41:59.000000', '2011-05-11 03:44:20.000000', 0),
(6410238, 949740, 96751, '<td valign="top">Now THAT''s out of the box thinking</td>', 'Now THAT''s out of the box thinking', '2011-05-11 03:46:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(6410240, 949724, 96751, '<td valign="top">This almost looks architectural.  And that score - I can''t believe it.  This deserved better.</td>', 'This almost looks architectural.  And that score - I can''t believe it.  This deserved better.', '2011-05-11 03:49:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(6410241, 949749, 96751, '<td valign="top">I''m going to have to try light painting one of these days.</td>', 'I''m going to have to try light painting one of these days.', '2011-05-11 03:50:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(6410242, 949542, 129267, '<td valign="top">i''m not sure if this is the case or not, but it makes sense in my head:<br/> <br/>for black/black without light reflections, you could use a piece of glass/acrylic that is lit from below. If you have a black card as your background it should reflect and create the black/black look, with intense color inside the glasses, and just a bit of a hairlight. <br/> <br/>here''s something I found:<br/> <br/>//www.photoblog.com/penguinphotos/2009/04/01/<br/> <br/></td>', 'i''m not sure if this is the case or not, but it makes sense in my head: for black/black without light reflections, you could use a piece of glass/acrylic that is lit from below. If you have a black card as your background it should reflect and create the black/black look, with intense color inside the glasses, and just a bit of a hairlight.  here''s something I found: //www.photoblog.com/penguinphotos/2009/04/01/ ', '2011-05-11 03:51:02.000000', NULL, 0),
